    "q-82016": {
      "dom_id": "step-q82016",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "If $\\overset{―}{R}=\\{m,a,t,h,s\\}$ and $\\overset{―}{S}=\\{s,e,t\\},$ then what is $\\overset{―}{R\\cup S}?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for unions states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{R\\cup S}≡\\overset{―}{R}\\cap \\overset{―}{S}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{R\\cup S} & =\\overset{―}{R}\\cap \\overset{―}{S} \\\\  & =\\{m,a,t,h,s\\}\\cap \\{s,e,t\\} \\\\  & =\\{s,t\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
