    "q-81867": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81867",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "If $\\overset{―}{A}=\\{x,y,z\\}$ and $\\overset{―}{B}=\\{w,x,y\\},$ then what is $\\overset{―}{A\\cup B}?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for unions states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A\\cup B}≡\\overset{―}{A}\\cap \\overset{―}{B}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A\\cup B} & =\\overset{―}{A}\\cap \\overset{―}{B} \\\\  & =\\{x,y,z\\}\\cap \\{w,x,y\\} \\\\  & =\\{x,y\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
