      "dom_id": "step-q102567",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "If $\\overset{―}{X}=\\{7,10,12,19,23\\}$ and $\\overset{―}{Y}=\\{8,10,12,14\\},$ then what is $\\overset{―}{X\\cup Y}?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for unions states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X\\cup Y}≡\\overset{―}{X}\\cap \\overset{―}{Y}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X\\cup Y} & =\\overset{―}{X}\\cap \\overset{―}{Y} \\\\  & =\\{7,10,12,19,23\\}\\cap \\{8,10,12,14\\} \\\\  & =\\{10,12\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
