      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "If $\\overset{―}{A}=\\{4,8,12\\}$ and $\\overset{―}{B}=\\{2,4,6\\},$ then what is $\\overset{―}{A\\cap B}?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for intersections states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A\\cap B}≡\\overset{―}{A}\\cup \\overset{―}{B}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A\\cap B} & =\\overset{―}{A}\\cup \\overset{―}{B} \\\\  & =\\{4,8,12\\}\\cup \\{2,4,6\\} \\\\  & =\\{2,4,6,8,12\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
