    "q-102569": {
      "dom_id": "step-q102569",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "If $\\overset{―}{R}=\\{{x}_{3},{x}_{5},{x}_{7},{x}_{11}\\}$ and $\\overset{―}{S}=\\{{x}_{4},{x}_{8},{x}_{13}\\},$ then what is $\\overset{―}{R\\cap S}?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for intersections states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{R\\cap S}≡\\overset{―}{R}\\cup \\overset{―}{S}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{R\\cap S} & =\\overset{―}{R}\\cup \\overset{―}{S} \\\\  & =\\{{x}_{3},{x}_{5},{x}_{7},{x}_{11}\\}\\cup \\{{x}_{4},{x}_{8},{x}_{13}\\} \\\\  & =\\{{x}_{3},{x}_{4},{x}_{5},{x}_{7},{x}_{8},{x}_{11},{x}_{13}\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
