    "q-82068": {
      "dom_id": "step-q82068",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "If $\\overset{―}{R}=\\{\\sqrt{2},\\pi ,e,\\sqrt{17}\\}$ and $\\overset{―}{S}=\\{\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{17}\\},$ then what is $\\overset{―}{R\\cap S}?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for intersections states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{R\\cap S}≡\\overset{―}{R}\\cup \\overset{―}{S}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{R\\cap S} & =\\overset{―}{R}\\cup \\overset{―}{S} \\\\  & =\\{\\sqrt{2},\\pi ,e,\\sqrt{17}\\}\\cup \\{\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{17}\\} \\\\  & =\\{\\sqrt{2},\\pi ,e,\\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{17}\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
