      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "If $\\overset{―}{P}=\\{3,5,7,12\\}$ and $\\overset{―}{Q}=\\{2,5,12\\},$ then what is $\\overset{―}{P\\cap Q}?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for intersections states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{P\\cap Q}≡\\overset{―}{P}\\cup \\overset{―}{Q}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{P\\cap Q} & =\\overset{―}{P}\\cup \\overset{―}{Q} \\\\  & =\\{3,5,7,12\\}\\cup \\{2,5,12\\} \\\\  & =\\{2,3,5,7,12\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
