      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "If $\\overset{―}{R}=\\{m,a,t,h\\}$ and $\\overset{―}{S}=\\{m,a,t,r,i,x\\},$ then what is $\\overset{―}{R\\cap S}?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for intersections states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{R\\cap S}≡\\overset{―}{R}\\cup \\overset{―}{S}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{R\\cap S} & =\\overset{―}{R}\\cup \\overset{―}{S} \\\\  & =\\{m,a,t,h\\}\\cup \\{m,a,t,r,i,x\\} \\\\  & =\\{m,a,t,h,r,i,x\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
